From 8cc53c0f7bfbaf6444e6e5c19232ec4a82d9e054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:43:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] board: zte: add ZXHN E2631 A1 RAM-chain support

Add the minimal board port for the ZTE ZXHN E2631 router (Sanechips
ZX279128S, dual Cortex-A9, 256 MiB DDR3, 128 MiB SPI-NAND).

This is the A1 stage: the image is loaded into RAM from the vendor
bootloader (tftp + go) and never written to flash. It provides:

  - DRAM sizing from the embedded device tree (256 MiB at 0x40000000)
  - a PL011 console at 0x94404000 with secondboot's 115200 8N1 setup
    kept intact (CFG_PL011_CLOCK is 0, so no baud rate programming)
  - the Cortex-A9 global timer, driven by a fixed 500 MHz a9_periph
    clock (CPU clock / 2)
  - TEXT_BASE 0x43000000 for the RAM chain; caches and MMU code stay
    off while the secondboot hand-off state is unknown
  - no SPI, NAND, environment or network support yet

The payload size budget for the later flash stages is 0x9F800 bytes:
secondboot copies the header length from mtd0 0x20800 and the payload
may run up to 0xBFFFF, with the environment area starting at 0xC0000.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
